{"title":"2018 USAJMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: For any geometry problem whose statement begins with an asterisk (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />), the first page of the solution must be a large, in-scale, clearly labeled diagram. Failure to meet this requirement will result in an automatic 1-point deduction. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, find the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit positive integers that satisfy both of the following conditions:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> no two consecutive digits are equal, and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> the last digit is a prime.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69ff720e6d0801983832367327a018e7afce9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=4\\sqrt[3]{abc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"21\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/7043a170ac5535465a5a1b4daccb1f1de3043280.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(ab+bc+ca)+4\\min(a^2,b^2,c^2)\\ge a^2+b^2+c^2.\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"20\" />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a quadrilateral inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39facf4ed73f7886f111ff2466878db18e5d8958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{BD}$\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> over lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681b31efa3f8f5c56418bc7cd02c79b356d180e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EPD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, and the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a77d6d11e0d217716222080a3c3ff7db9ab792be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle FPD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f772581ab4a0fe76335c6f85284d783ceb810134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EQ = FR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: For any geometry problem whose statement begins with an asterisk (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />), the first page of the solution must be a large, in-scale, clearly labeled diagram. Failure to meet this requirement will result in an automatic 1-point deduction. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in a circle of radius 2 with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/4466efb3f77dcf12e2ba1824beab88921fd77456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC \\geq 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number satisfying the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d467362fb90b2ef6c013f2aecb87221bb36614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 + ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d508f8eb94bbdf574b282ebec0cc12a4d5c0a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=BC,b=CA,c=AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"197\" height=\"16\" />. Find all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c3130ada36271a164087102045c119516fdfea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, \\dots, a_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> be integers. Show that there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that the numbers\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7624ce20fc9bfb798126ffacdb34110159ef0094.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1 + k, a_2 + 2k, \\dots, a_p + pk\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"17\" />produce at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94a56b75241f2eb79c48ba67c5bc24948152cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2} p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"19\" height=\"21\" /> distinct remainders upon division by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Karl starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cards labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358dbb70c4ab6fcd474f3cb6877588af5fcb9ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,\\dots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> lined up in a random order on his desk. He calls a pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> of these cards swapped if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and the card labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is to the left of the card labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. For instance, in the sequence of cards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b964153b9a685c97096663b27bad359dbe96e287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,1,4,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, there are three swapped pairs of cards, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04c2d1bd65c882efed8513bbbf77022aba66364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8790f46883a296366f038323844601dd2cde9ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb9265e7854534e5c082e16eb10470d08d46e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>He picks up the card labeled 1 and inserts it back into the sequence in the opposite position: if the card labeled 1 had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> card to its left, then it now has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> cards to its right. He then picks up the card labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and reinserts it in the same manner, and so on until he has picked up and put back each of the cards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/838228ac8ee711eda2bdae0818393f87407dbc66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,\\dots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> exactly once in that order. (For example, the process starting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b964153b9a685c97096663b27bad359dbe96e287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,1,4,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/9990bd27940b1c17121b0c9887faa3131ac6eb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,1,4,2\\to 3,4,1,2\\to 2,3,4,1\\to 2,4,3,1\\to 2,3,4,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"415\" height=\"16\" />.)\n</p><p>Show that, no matter what lineup of cards Karl started with, his final lineup has the same number of swapped pairs as the starting lineup.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO\" title=\"2018 USAJMO\">2018 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems\">2017 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems\">2019 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018001831\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 315/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 84/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10186/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.631      1 -total\n 52.79%    6.668      1 Template:USAJMO_box\n 45.51%    5.748      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16178:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018001831 and revision id 196455. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}